# L §5.11: "missing(r), r a read of an input (LOAD-MISSING otherwise)"; L §8.3's text "missing(<r>): <r> is not a read
# of an input". p is a def. (Writer 6: was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §5.11.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

input pnl[d in days]: num
def p[d in days]: num = pnl[d] at d

def gone[d in days]: bool at d
  rule base v v1 = false
  rule no_record beats base v v1 = true when missing(p[d])

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  pnl[2026-03-02] = 1 "s"
=== expect
refused: LOAD-MISSING missing(p[d]): p[d] is not a read of an input ...
